From: Stanislav Malyshev <stas@php.net>
Date: Sun Aug 7 16:17:54 2016 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Fix bug #72771: ftps:// opendir wrapper is vulnerable to protocol downgrade attack

5.5 backport: https://github.com/shivammathur/php-src-backports/commit/bd925690792e765128876e55cd05e9062b8bad6f
---
diff --git a/ext/standard/ftp_fopen_wrapper.c b/ext/standard/ftp_fopen_wrapper.c
--- a/ext/standard/ftp_fopen_wrapper.c
+++ b/ext/standard/ftp_fopen_wrapper.c
@@ -186,7 +186,8 @@ static php_stream *php_ftp_fopen_connect(php_stream_wrapper *wrapper, char *path
 			/* get the response */
 			result = GET_FTP_RESULT(stream);
 			if (result != 334) {
-				use_ssl = 0;
+				php_stream_wrapper_log_error(wrapper, options TSRMLS_CC, "Server doesn't support FTPS.");
+				goto connect_errexit;
 			} else {
 				/* we must reuse the old SSL session id */
 				/* if we talk to an old ftpd-ssl */
